cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Analysis of a Legacy DBL Accounting System (1980-2026)"
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Parsons
    given-names: Noah
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7224-6040"
abstract: >-
  Documentation and analysis tooling produced during the preservation of a
  multi-module accounting system written in DBL, in continuous production use
  from 1980 until 2026. Includes a technical report describing the preservation
  method and its verification, an extracted schema of 339 record layouts and
  2,425 fields, a dependency map of 2,567 program-to-record relationships, an
  authorship analysis, and the parser used to generate the schema.
keywords:
  - software preservation
  - legacy systems
  - DBL
  - DIBOL
  - Synergy/DE
  - reproducible builds
  - digital archaeology
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-09-06"
